\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\sb100\sa100\b Equations to Calculate The Median Voltage at the Input of the Receiver\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\qj\b0 Ohm's Law: \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx0\tx959\tx1918\tx2877\tx3836\tx4795\tx5754\tx6713\tx7672\tx8631\par
E = I*R or I = E/R\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\qj\par
Power formula: \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx0\tx959\tx1918\tx2877\tx3836\tx4795\tx5754\tx6713\tx7672\tx8631\par
P = EI\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\qj\par
P is in Watts, E is in Volts and I is in Amps and R is in Ohms. \par
\lang1031 Then: \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx0\tx959\tx1918\tx2877\tx3836\tx4795\tx5754\tx6713\tx7672\tx8631\par
P = E * [E/R] = (E^2)/R\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\qj\par
Solve for Voltage: \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx0\tx959\tx1918\tx2877\tx3836\tx4795\tx5754\tx6713\tx7672\tx8631\par
E^2  = [P*R]\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\qj\par
Convert to dB: \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx0\tx959\tx1918\tx2877\tx3836\tx4795\tx5754\tx6713\tx7672\tx8631\par
10 Log E^2 = 20 Log E = 10 Log [P*R]\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\qj\par
\lang1033 Express E in terms of microVolts such that E(V) = E (uV) x 10^6, then: \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx0\tx959\tx1918\tx2877\tx3836\tx4795\tx5754\tx6713\tx7672\tx8631\par
\lang1031 20 Log E + 20 Log [ 1V / 10^6]  =  10 Log [P*R]\par
\par
E(dBuV) - 120   =  10 Log P + 10 Log R\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\qj\par
Assume R = 50 Ohms: \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx0\tx959\tx1918\tx2877\tx3836\tx4795\tx5754\tx6713\tx7672\tx8631\par
E(dBuV) - 120   =  10 Log P  + 10 Log (50 Ohms) = P(dBW) + 17\par
\par
E(dBuV) =  P(dBW) + 17 + 120 = P(dBW) + 137\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\qj\par
\lang1033 Finally, E in uV is 10^(dBuV/20) or antilog [(dBuV)/20]. Example: 35 dBuV = 10^(35/20) = 56 uV. \par
\par
NOTE: VOACAP computes the signal power [S DBW] which is equivalent to the P(dBW) in the above equations. DO NOT confuse the predicted field strength in the VOACAP output, DBU (dB relative to 1 microVolt per meter), with the voltage at the receiver as given by dBuV (dB relative to 1 microVolt) in the above equations.\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-760\li760\ri-1800\qj\par
